  "notes": "どっち is the casual form of どちら, used to ask \"which one\" (of two) or \"which way.\"\n\nKO-SO-A-DO SERIES:\n- こっち: this way / this one (near speaker)\n- そっち: that way / that one (near listener)\n- あっち: over there / that one (far from both)\n- どっち: which way / which one (question)\n\nFORMALITY:\n- どっち: casual (used with friends, family)\n- どちら: polite (used in formal situations, with strangers)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- どっちがいい？: Which one is better?\n- どっちでもいい: Either is fine.\n- どっちにする？: Which will you choose?\n- どっちかというと: if I had to choose / rather\n\nNOTE:\nUsed for choosing between two options. For three or more, use どれ (casual) or どれか.",
